    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Process restarts",
      "description": "One spike per replica per process start. Reads the recorded start timestamp against the step window rather than counting counter resets: a Deployment restart is a NEW series, not a reset of the old one, so `resets()` never fired here.\n\n**The one signal that explains a simultaneous gap in every other series** -- and the one the hop gaps and `Replica fan-out` both tell you to go and check.\n\nLegend: `{{service_instance_id}}`\n\n**`>= bool`, so every live replica always holds a line.** A bare comparison drops the series between restarts and Grafana renders \"No data\" -- indistinguishable from a broken panel, which is the failure this whole fix exists to remove. `bool` keeps each replica at a flat 0 and lifts it to 1 for one rate-interval when that process started.",
